/**
@example main.c
@details A word counter built on the single header, dist/mule.h. The file
lives in a Str inside an Arena, and every line and word is a StrView into it.

@example checked_math.c
@details base: size arithmetic with ckd_mul() and ckd_add(), so an overflow
is caught before it reaches malloc.

@example arena_scratch.c
@details mem: one Arena per request, rewound with a mark, so a batch of
strings frees in one call.

@example todo_list.c
@details arr: a growable array of structs, with push, insert, remove and pop.

@example inventory.c
@details map: tally items by name, list them in first-seen order, and remove
one.

@example why_it_failed.c
@details err: fill an Err in your own function, and branch on its kind rather
than its text.

@example dice.c
@details rand: two dice rolled from a fixed seed, so every run prints the same
histogram.

@example stopwatch.c
@details time: time a loop with time_now_ns().

@example logging.c
@details log: levelled messages that carry their file and line, filtered at
run time.

@example unit_tests.c
@details test: unit tests for code of your own, with leak checks and an
allocation that fails on purpose.

@example line_count.c
@details fs: walk a tree in sorted order and read each file to count its
lines.

@example run_commands.c
@details proc: capture a command's output, see how a failure is reported, and
run jobs in a ProcPool.

@example cli_options.c
@details args: options, positionals and a generated `--help` from one table.

@example project/build.c
@details build: a project's build as a C program that rebuilds itself and
recompiles only what changed.

@example 01_build.c
@details Build a Str with appends that chain with `&&`, print it two ways,
free it.

@example 02_reuse.c
@details Clear and refill one Str in a loop, so one allocation serves every
pass.

@example 03_file.c
@details Read a whole file into a Str, and tell a read error from out of
memory.

@example 04_views.c
@details Trim, find and slice a StrView without allocating, and see why `%s`
is the wrong way to print one.

@example 05_split.c
@details Split fields with sv_split_next() and words with sv_token_next(),
and see how they treat empty pieces.

@example 06_sort.c
@details Sort an array of StrViews with qsort and sv_cmp().

@example 07_lines.c
@details One Str owns a whole novel, and views walk its 22,750 lines without
a single further allocation.

@example 08_keep.c
@details Copy a view into a Str of its own when the text must outlive the
buffer it came from.

@example 09_replace.c
@details Write your own function in the library's shape: StrViews in, a Str
to append to, a `bool` out.

@example 10_dangling.c
@details A bug on purpose. A view kept across an append that moves the
buffer reads freed memory.

@example 11_double_free.c
@details A bug on purpose. Copying a Str struct makes two owners of one
buffer.
*/
